  "credit": "@curlytales",
  "notes": "Speech was too garbled to read, so amounts come from the words I could pick out (3/4 cup water, 1/2 tsp salt, 1/2 tsp sugar, a little lime juice) and from the frames; the besan (2 scoops of a wooden cup) and beetroot are my estimates. Steaming time, flame level and greasing the tin are not shown. The pale seeds in the tadka are not clear (look like yellow mustard). The Eno step shows the sachet being poured; mixing it in is not shown, so mix gently and steam quickly."
